**Five-step system for business owners:**

1. **Targeting (ICP)** — Demographics + problems/goals. Fill in: "I help [ideal viewer] transition from [pain] to [goal] so they can [impact]."

2. **Ideation** — Sparking (no data) vs Spotting (find proven outlier videos in/adjacent niche, adapt for ICP). Spotting preferred.

3. **Packaging** — Title + thumbnail. Target 5.5%+ CTR. Title ≤55 chars. BENS system: Big claim, Easy, New, Safe (need 3/4).

4. **Value (HIVE formula)** — Hook (repeat title expectation, ≤30s) → Intro (credibility, ≤30s) → Value (3-5 points, give away everything) → End screen. "On YouTube, you are as good as you communicate."

5. **Money** — **500 targeted views = 1 lead.** Two CTAs: at 3-5 min and at 70-80%. CTA at top of description + pinned comment.

**Core principle:** Niche down to blow up. Small channel with 500 views/video targeting ideal buyers beats 1.5M sub entertainment channel for revenue.

**Example:** Jamon — Oxford/Cambridge maths niche, $250K/year, ~500 views/video.


